## 3. The Resolution & Gatekeeper Engine (Service Layer)

The true power of this module lies in `services/settings/settings_service.py`. It provides 3 critical backend mechanics:

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hierarchical Resolution:** 
> When the `ReportingService` generates a PDF, it calls `resolve_setting("reporting", "global_header_template")`. The engine will check the **Campaign** for a custom header. If missing, it checks the **Group**. If missing, it checks the **Global User** settings. If missing, it falls back to the hardcoded KapuLetu Default.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Subscription Feature Gating:** 
> Users cannot hack the API to unlock premium features. When a `PUT` request is made to enable `auto_approve_enabled` or `remove_kapuletu_branding`, the service triggers `_enforce_feature_gate()`. This dynamically queries the `Subscription` table, checks the user's active Plan feature limits, and explicitly blocks the request with a `402 Payment Required` if they are unauthorized.

> [!TIP]
> **Cross-Module DB Syncing:** 
> When a user toggles `auto_renew_subscription` in the Settings API, the Service instantly executes a database `UPDATE` on the `subscriptions` table. This ensures the `expiry_worker.py` (which handles downgrades) is perfectly synchronized with the user's settings.

