## 4. UI-Mapped API Endpoints

To prevent the frontend from having to send massive, clashing JSON payloads, `services/settings/router.py` exposes exactly **14 independent, button-mapped endpoints**.

### Global User Level
1. `GET /settings/me`: Fetches the entire settings blob for initial UI rendering.
2. `PUT /settings/me/security/2fa`: Dedicated endpoint for the 2FA toggle.
3. `PUT /settings/me/security/timeout`: Dedicated endpoint for the timeout slider.
4. `PUT /settings/me/automation/auto-approve`: Dedicated endpoint for the AI auto-approve toggle *(Gated)*.
5. `PUT /settings/me/automation/fallback`: Dedicated endpoint for the fallback routing dropdown.
6. `PUT /settings/me/reports/frequency`: Dedicated endpoint for report scheduling dropdown.
7. `PUT /settings/me/reports/branding`: Dedicated endpoint for headers/footers *(Gated)*.
8. `PUT /settings/me/regional/localization`: Dedicated endpoint for currency/timezone dropdowns.
9. `PUT /settings/me/notifications/alerts`: Dedicated endpoint for large transaction thresholds.
10. `PUT /settings/me/billing`: Dedicated endpoint for auto-renew toggles (syncs with Subscriptions DB).

### Group Level (Overrides)
11. `GET /groups/{group_id}/settings`: Fetches local overrides.
12. `PUT /groups/{group_id}/settings/reports`: Overrides the header/footer just for this Group.
13. `PUT /groups/{group_id}/settings/automation`: Overrides automation routing just for this Group.

### Campaign Level (Overrides)
14. `GET /campaigns/{campaign_id}/settings`: Fetches local overrides.
15. `PUT /campaigns/{campaign_id}/settings/reports`: Sets a specific `public_ledger_pin` strictly for this campaign.

All endpoints are mounted on the root FastAPI instance in `local_server.py` and are officially documented in the Swagger UI under the **"17. Enterprise Settings"** tag.
